= Choosing a Race =

See [[Choosing a Race]].

=Faction Alignment=

A brief explanation:

* Races that are <i>Good</i> can typically enter other <i>Good</i> cities without being attacked.
* Races that are <i>Evil</i> can typically enter other <i>Evil</i> cities without being attacked.
* <i>Neutral</i> races can typically enter any city, and <i>Good/Evil</i> races can typically enter theirs.
* Iksar are hated by every race, and other races will likely be attacked upon entering their city.
* There ARE other factors, including Deity and Class choice, completed quests, etc.

=* Listed below are all of the innate (non-skill) racials: *=
==Barrel Roll==
Male Dwarves have a unique jump animation, and while it is purely cosmetic (ie. has no in-game benefit), it ''is'' pretty cool.

==Cursed Heritage==
10% increased effectiveness of taps and runes. 20% reduced base health regen when outdoors in the day.

Cursed Heritage works on: 
* DD Lifetap Spells
* DD Lifetap Procs (both weapon and VE)
* Cast Runes
* Click Runes (Bladestopper)

Cursed Heritage stacks with Improved Vampirism III or Improved Damage III with:
* DD Lifetap Spells
* DD Lifetap Procs (Weapon only, not VE)

Cursed Heritage does not work on: 
* DoT Lifetaps
* Berserker Blood Runes

==Frontal Stun Immunity==
[[Ogre|Ogres]] cannot be stunned from the front, which gives them an advantage over other races.

* Enemy attacks can still push you backwards, which will interrupt your spell casting.
* Tip: You can stand in a corner to avoid being pushed back.
* Enemy attacks still have a chance to interrupt on hit. This chance is increased on some attacks such as bash.
Steadfast Will is an [[Alternate Advancement|AA]] you can purchase that gives you Stun Immunity.

==Increased Armor Class==
[[Iksar]] start with a +15 AC bonus (+17 if they are a [[Warrior]]) over other races, which scales with level, increasing up to a maximum of +35.

==Increased Consumption Rate==
[[Barbarian]]s, [[Halfling]]s, [[Ogre]]s, and [[Troll]]s all consume one unit of food and drink every 30 mins, while the remaining races consume one per hour.

